From: PlayThing builder <builder@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] omx: register the PlayThing hardware H.264 decoder

Adds "OMX.google.cpt.h264.decoder" to the soft codec table. The component is
in device/spotify/superbird/codecs/cpth264dec (libstagefright_soft_cpth264dec):
it decodes H.264 on the Amlogic hardware decoder through V4L2 (/dev/video26)
and gives I420 frames like OMX.google.h264.decoder. The "OMX.google." prefix
keeps the software renderer path in ACodec and MediaCodec.

---
diff --git a/media/libstagefright/omx/SoftOMXPlugin.cpp b/media/libstagefright/omx/SoftOMXPlugin.cpp
index 1f3e8c1..5b841b9 100644
--- a/media/libstagefright/omx/SoftOMXPlugin.cpp
+++ b/media/libstagefright/omx/SoftOMXPlugin.cpp
@@ -46,6 +46,8 @@ static const struct {
     { "OMX.google.amrwb.decoder", "amrdec", "audio_decoder.amrwb" },
     { "OMX.google.amrwb.encoder", "amrwbenc", "audio_encoder.amrwb" },
     { "OMX.google.h264.decoder", "avcdec", "video_decoder.avc" },
+    // PlayThing: H.264 on the Amlogic hardware decoder (device/spotify/superbird).
+    { "OMX.google.cpt.h264.decoder", "cpth264dec", "video_decoder.avc" },
     { "OMX.google.h264.encoder", "avcenc", "video_encoder.avc" },
     { "OMX.google.hevc.decoder", "hevcdec", "video_decoder.hevc" },
     { "OMX.google.g711.alaw.decoder", "g711dec", "audio_decoder.g711alaw" },
